{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_e1f62cdbc52d3b4bf458147a10b67e1a8cc36469b567d0a9245ff0bc4239254e", "title": "José Feliciano", "text": "José Montserrate Feliciano García (born September 10, 1945), better known simply as José Feliciano ] , is a Puerto Rican guitarist, singer, and songwriter, best known for many international hits, including his rendition of The Doors' \"Light My Fire\" and the best-selling Christmas single, \"Feliz Navidad\". His music is known for having a mix of styles, for example including both flamenco music and mellow easy listening influences in many songs.", "score": 11.9712}, {"id": "hp_doc_c16953fb513ee8fa4fc872dc95a19ea057963d16d2077176fc7bd82b4bf4e7d4", "title": "Romance in the Night", "text": "Romance in the Night is a soft rock album of mostly covers by José Feliciano. It was released after the return of his historic hit producer Rick Jarrard on the Motown label in 1983. The track \"Let’s Find Each Other Tonight” (a Feliciano original) was his first single to make the Country charts and was played by the same José Feliciano live on the 1996 movie \"Fargo\" by the Coen brothers .", "score": 11.8387}, {"id": "hp_doc_6c9d0426f16387a5b400cb82c7a907e6c7fcb027ba99ba8e8bd68787252434b2", "title": "Jose Prakash", "text": "Jose Prakash (14 April 1925 – 24 March 2012) was an Indian actor and singer who worked in Malayalam cinema. He was a singer turned actor who had appeared in more than 300 films mostly in antagonist roles. He was awarded with the J. C. Daniel Award for 2011 a day before he died aged 87.", "score": 9.6047}], "remaining_searches": 1}
